    <description>Checks, before RLM_ConsolidateRenewalOpportunities renews anything, whether any of the given root assets has an asset state period in a time zone other than GMT (a period with no time zone uses GMT) or in a ramp, whether a quote on any opportunity, open or closed, would renew one of their current terms, and whether any of the given opportunities already has a quote. Runs in system context without sharing: Start End Time Zone and the ramp fields on Asset State Period are usually hidden by field-level security, which would fail a read in user context, and a quote the user can't see could still be ordered and renew the same assets. It is given the root assets and opportunities the caller already read and returns only a yes or no for each check, never a record, an Id or a field value.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <description>A renew line's quote action and its exact start.</description>
        <name>RenewLineKey</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>{!Loop_Renew_Lines.QuoteActionId} &amp; "@" &amp; TEXT({!Loop_Renew_Lines.StartDateTime})</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>The key a line of this quote action would have if it renewed the asset's current term, which starts the second after the asset ends.</description>
        <name>PendingRenewalKey</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>{!Loop_Pending_Actions.Id} &amp; "@" &amp; TEXT({!Loop_Action_Assets.LifecycleEndDate} + 1/86400)</expression>
    </formulas>
    <interviewLabel>RLM Renewal Preflight Checks {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>RLM Renewal Preflight Checks</label>
    <loops>
